{#
  Phase 2: advertise UDN pod subnets into the DEFAULT VRF.

  Leaving targetVRF unset leaks each selected UDN's routes into the node's
  default VRF, where the existing untagged BGP session picks them up. No
  VLANs, no per-tenant VRFs, no NMState - which is exactly why this phase is
  worth doing before VRF-Lite: it isolates "does UDN-over-BGP work" from
  "does my VLAN and VRF plumbing work".

  The cost of the simplicity is real and should be stated: leaking a UDN into
  the default VRF gives up the UDN's isolation at the node boundary. Anything
  else in that VRF can now reach these pods.

  It also means two UDNs leaked here may not carry the same subnet - one
  prefix in one VRF cannot mean two things. OVN-Kubernetes does NOT check
  that; its route advertisements controller has a literal
  `// TODO check overlaps?` where the validation would go, so overlapping
  subnets are Accepted and produce one winner and one silently unreachable
  tenant. Hence udn_subnet_shared, and the assert in main.yml.
#}
apiVersion: k8s.ovn.org/v1
kind: RouteAdvertisements
metadata:
  name: udn-shared-vrf
spec:
  # targetVRF is deliberately left unset, and unset is not the same as
  # "default". An empty targetVRF means "advertise in the default VRF"; a
  # non-empty one is matched LITERALLY against the vrf field of the routers
  # in the selected FRRConfiguration. Writing 'default' therefore makes
  # OVN-Kubernetes look for a 'router bgp <asn> vrf default', find none -
  # a router with no vrf field IS the default VRF, it is not named - and
  # reject the CR with "has no VRF matching the RouteAdvertisements target
  # VRF or any selected network". 'auto' is the only other accepted value.
  networkSelectors:
    - networkSelectionType: ClusterUserDefinedNetworks
      clusterUserDefinedNetworkSelector:
        networkSelector:
          matchLabels:
            {{ udn_bgp_cudn_label_key }}: "enabled"
  nodeSelector: {}
  frrConfigurationSelector:
    matchLabels:
      {{ udn_bgp_frr_label_key }}: fabric-default
  advertisements:
    - PodNetwork
